# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# Gemini API key and per-plugin credentials
config/api_keys.json
!config/api_keys.example.json
# Gemini web session cookies (optional, for Pro model access — never commit!)
config/gemini_cookies.json
# LLM response cache (SQLite, regenerated automatically)
config/llm_cache.db
# Dashboard TLS private key and certificate
config/certs/
# Linked WhatsApp session
config/whatsapp_web/
# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/token*.json
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/user_persona.json
memory/reflections.json
memory/journals/
memory/obsidian_vault/
memory/*.db
memory/*.sqlite*
memory/*.jsonl
# SQLite in WAL mode creates sidecar files next to the database. `*.db` above
# does not match these, so they were getting committed.
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*-shm
*-wal
memory/contacts.json
memory/corrections.json
memory/feedback.json
memory/learned_intents.json
memory/tinydb_store.json
# Learned graph of the user's own people and relationships. Personal by
# nature, and regenerated on demand: memory/knowledge_graph.py._load() returns
# an empty graph when the file is absent and _save() recreates it, so a fresh
# clone starts blank and builds its own. See knowledge_graph.example.json.
config/knowledge_graph.json
config/weather_cache.json
# Per-user runtime config: their own routines, and the keywords their privacy
# shield watches for. Both are written by normal use, both describe the person
# running it rather than the software, and neither is needed for a fresh clone
# to work. See routines.example.json and privacy_settings.example.json.
config/routines.json
config/privacy_settings.json
config/installed_apps.json
config/music_library.json
config/todos.json
config/agent_plans.json
config/active_timers.json
config/scheduled_jobs.json
Desktop/
config/*.sqlite*
config/*.db

# ── Large Neural Models & Voice Weights ────────────────────────────────────────
*.onnx
*.tflite
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.gguf
models/
core/models/piper/*
!core/models/piper/.gitkeep

# ── Generated SFX & Audio Cache ───────────────────────────────────────────────
core/assets/sfx/*.wav
*.mp3
*.wav
!core/assets/sfx/.gitkeep

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output & Temporary Files ──────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.bak-*
config/*.bak-*
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
scratch/
cache/
config/generated_sniffers/*.py
config/swarm_outputs/*.json
node_modules/

# Theme choice made on one machine - 'preset', text size and density are personal
# preference, not source, and committing it ships the user's UI settings to every fork.
# Written by core/theme.py on first save; see core/theme.py for the defaults.
config/ui_theme.json
